  <reporting-org ref="XI-IATI-IADB" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inter-American Development Bank</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Consolidacin de un sector elctrico sostenible</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consolidating a Sustainable Energy Sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">El objetivo general es potenciar el desarrollo econmico rural asegurando un acceso adecuado y moderno a la electricidad sostenible para mejorar las condiciones de vida de la poblacin rural y tambin el entorno de negocios rural con un mejor suministro de electricidad como servicio pblico. Los objetivos especficos son los siguientes: (i) promover la ejecucin de la reforma energtica brindando apoyo a la Direccin de Energa de Suriname (EAS) y la gestin operativa de EBS; (ii) incrementar la fiabilidad del sistema de energa y promover la diversificacin de la matriz energtica mediante el financiamiento de actividades previas a la inversin relacionadas con energa renovable y gas natural; y (iii) ampliar la cobertura de electricidad mediante la extensin de la red y sistemas fuera de la red y un mayor suministro de sistemas de energa renovable.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The general objective is to improve rural economic development, by ensuring adequate and modern access to sustainable electricity to enhance the living conditions of the rural population while improving the rural business environment with better provision of electricity as a public service. The specific objectives are to: (i) advance the implementation of energy reform through support to the Energy Authority of Suriname (EAS) and operational management of the EBS; (ii) increase the reliability of the power system and promote the diversification of the energy matrix through financing pre-investment activities related to Renewable Energy (RE) and Natural Gas (NG); and (iii) expand electricity coverage through a combination of grid extension and off-grid- systems, increasing the provision of RE systems</narrative>
  </description>
